<hr>



<div class="row">
    <div class="col">


        <h2>Do Freelancers Need to Issue GST Invoice?</h2>

        <p>Freelancers must issue GST invoices if they are registered under GST. GST registration becomes mandatory when annual turnover exceeds:</p>

        <ul>
            <li>₹20 lakh for most states</li>
            <li>₹10 lakh for special category states</li>
        </ul>

        <p>Even if turnover is below this limit, some freelancers voluntarily register for GST because clients may require a GST invoice.</p>

        <hr>

        <h2>What Should a Freelancer GST Invoice Include?</h2>

        <p>A GST invoice issued by freelancers must include the following mandatory details:</p>

        <ul>
            <li>Freelancer name and address</li>
            <li>GSTIN (if registered)</li>
            <li>Unique invoice number</li>
            <li>Invoice date</li>
            <li>Client name and address</li>
            <li>Client GSTIN (if applicable)</li>
            <li>Description of services</li>
            <li>SAC code</li>
            <li>Taxable value</li>
            <li>GST rate applied</li>
            <li>CGST / SGST or IGST amount</li>
            <li>Total invoice value</li>
            <li>Place of supply</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="col">

        <h2>SAC Code for Freelancers</h2>

        <p>Freelancers providing services must use <strong>SAC (Services Accounting Code)</strong> instead of HSN codes.</p>

        <p>Common SAC codes used by freelancers:</p>

        <ul>
            <li>998313 – IT consulting services</li>
            <li>998314 – Software development services</li>
            <li>998361 – Advertising and marketing services</li>
            <li>998391 – Professional consulting services</li>
        </ul>

        <p>Correct SAC code ensures proper GST classification and compliance.</p>

        <hr>

        <h2>GST Rate for Freelance Services</h2>

        <p>Most freelance services are taxed at <strong>18% GST</strong>.</p>

        <h4>Example GST Calculation</h4>

        <p>Freelance project value: ₹30,000</p>

        <ul>
            <li>CGST 9% = ₹2,700</li>
            <li>SGST 9% = ₹2,700</li>
        </ul>

        <p><strong>Total Invoice Value = ₹35,400</strong></p>

        <p>If the client is located in another state:</p>

        <ul>
            <li>IGST 18% = ₹5,400</li>
        </ul>

        <hr>

        <h4>Intra-State vs Inter-State GST for Freelancers</h4>
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col">
                <h5>Same State Client</h5>

                <p>Freelancer and client located in the same state:</p>

                <ul>
                    <li>CGST + SGST applied</li>
                </ul>

            </div>
            <div class="col">
                <h5>Different State Client</h5>

                <p>If client is in another state:</p>

                <ul>
                    <li>IGST is applied</li>
                </ul>

            </div>
        </div>


    </div>
</div>


